- At an exhibition at the House of Culture in Něvský, where my works were exhibited.
I've understood what my path is.
That's when a wave of old free unofficial artists passed over, and I couldn't understand the new, unmarried types of artists.
I befriended the artists of the new wave, the post-Gazonevians, who brought us to "Pushkini 10," and there weren't other waves.
It appeals to theatre, dressing, music, all genres except the word.
- And all of this merged in your art-clinic ...- It was important for me to find myself in the center of the culture of Peterburk, where all the best forces of creativity should be gathered.
In 1995, I took a place on Pushkin 10, and even before the reconstruction, there was a musical-art club, a bohemian club, the home of the Peterburk bohemia.
