Šnur and his friends sang light songs under plywood, dressed in close-fitting jerseys, in the middle among them the composer Igor Vdovin, who is now in vogue.
When the band started playing live, it became "Leningrad."
Trachtenberg led a lot of Hali-Galivian time programs.
We gave them Trachtenberg, thus beginning his great career, basic education and vocational training from us.
Gallery "D 137", club "Gribojedov - this is the reverberation of the Art Clinic.
That's where our workers and regular guests left.
I'm a hero of the last century when culture still meant something.
In 2000, a survey was held in the press, a special prize was "People in Our City."
In the "Artist of the Year" nomination, I was appointed, thus ending my peak.
In the new times according to the old rules, work is unpleasant, I am a man of truth, honesty and culture of the last century.
In the current years it is easy to become popular, but culture and popularity are various things today, you can be popular, but not very cultural.
- Your works are characterized in a recognizable way.
- Many of my paintings - these are hits in which topicality and penetrability are vividly captured.
I'll have a program exhibition "Russian Clown Museum."
Clowns are a timeless category.
I used to be sociable, today being like this is painful and terrible.
But in clowns, everything is blurring, the tragic is being sensed.
I love grotesque, I have grotesque ideas.
For example, to save the world by way of totalitarianism in the order.
Today, people meet according to their clothes, oriented towards external mechanics, not on the inner person.
Or maybe you can't shake his hand and you have to spit in his face.
And the deception will be eliminated by changing.
- We've seen you in the role of a city bottler recently. - A cultural city should have such a hero.
And who should he be if it wasn't me?
- And can commercial art be beautiful?
- At the moment, the commercial, utile art should be thorough, tactful, sweet.
There is a disintegration of cultures.
Previously, people used to come together in clusters, bohemians loved one, simple other people.
Today, everything has broken down on micro-company, today it's very hard to please everyone.
I'm not a hundred-dollar bill to please everyone.
You have to think about who you'll like today.
Today, every cultural hero has his 100 fans.
- And several thousand spectators will come to Stasu Mikhailova!
There's a fans coming at him, that's where the sexually social sphere gets involved.
And 300 people come to the cultural ground, and 10 thousand of them don't come, and the result is less management, money, everything withers.
I've got fans, the main thing is that no one deceives them and violates what's ingrained.
When I was young, I painted pictures hanging from a collector on the wall, along with Falk and Larionov.
I started with paintings by which people usually end up.
Nowadays, people often confuse concepts.
They say:Clergy culture, consumer culture.
There's no consumer culture, it's from elsewhere.
I'm a man of yesterday's culture, I grew up on examples by artists who lived in poverty and died in poverty, refusing money for drawing paintings.
And I'm for that kind of culture.
Cyril, what's scarce in Petersburg?
- Good culture experts.
There is such a concept: an official through culture.
However, not everyone can deal with culture.
It wasn't like this in everything in the days of the Ordinary Tsars, the Tsars may not have understood the culture very much, but they understood that real experts needed to be promoted.
There are good consultants in Moscow today.
Here in St. Petersburg we have people who could be experts, but they are tucked away somewhere in the corner, because there are a need for great experts, who rightly appreciate these experts and put them on the right path.
Today, Taste is thriving.
The same Erarta, but it differs in that they sincerely say that not all modern art we accept, there are artists who should be looking for other museums.
- What do you think is Petersburg?
- St. Petersburg - it is not the capital of culture, there is much more culture in Moscow, there is the right soil.
And on our eels, art thrives poorly.
